# Activity: Daily Dashboard Component (Routines & Habits Integration)

## 1. Objective & Context
Develop the central, unified Daily Dashboard view (`DashboardView.vue`). The dashboard integrates the active Routine time block schedule with the daily Habit Tracker, displaying a real-time progress gauge and enabling one-tap check-ins.

- **Prerequisites:** Activities 01 and 02 of Feature 09.
- **Target Location:** `frontend/src/views/DashboardView.vue` and `frontend/src/components/dashboard/`.

## 2. Technical Scope & Specifications
- **Components:**
  - `RoutineTimeline.vue`: Vertical or horizontal schedule highlighting the currently active block with glowing indicator and countdown to next block.
  - `HabitChecklist.vue`: Interactive list of today's habits with one-tap toggle for binary habits and quick incremental stepper for numeric habits (e.g. `+250ml`).
  - `DailyProgressGauge.vue`: Radial or linear progress indicator combining routine and habit completion rates.
- **Micro-Animations:** Smooth state transitions using Vue `<TransitionGroup>` and CSS keyframes.

## 3. UI Component Architecture

```
frontend/src/components/dashboard/
├── DailyProgressGauge.vue
├── RoutineTimeline.vue
├── TimeBlockCard.vue
├── HabitChecklist.vue
└── HabitCheckinRow.vue
```

### Dashboard View Wireframe Structure (`DashboardView.vue`)
```vue
<template>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 space-y-8">
    <!-- Top Summary Banner -->
    <header class="flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-between items-start md:items-center gap-4">
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Daily Focus</h1>
        <p class="text-slate-400 mt-1">{{ currentDateFormatted }}</p>
      </div>
      <DailyProgressGauge :percentage="combinedProgressPercentage" />
    </header>

    <!-- Main Grid: Routines (Left) & Habits (Right) -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8">
      <section class="lg:col-span-7 bg-surface-card border border-surface-border rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Routine Schedule</h2>
        <RoutineTimeline :blocks="routineBlocks" @complete="onCompleteBlock" />
      </section>

      <section class="lg:col-span-5 bg-surface-card border border-surface-border rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Today's Habits</h2>
        <HabitChecklist :habits="dailyHabits" @checkin="onHabitCheckin" />
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>
```

## 4. Implementation Steps
1. Create `frontend/src/components/dashboard/` components.
2. Connect `useRoutineStore` and `useHabitStore` in `DashboardView.vue`.
3. Implement real-time interval timer (`setInterval` every 60s) to update active time block styling.
4. Implement one-tap optimistic UI updates on habit check-ins: immediately mark UI as completed while transmitting POST request in background.

## 5. Security, Error Handling & Edge Cases
- **Optimistic Rollback:** If the network request fails, revert the check-in UI state and display a toast alert.
- **Empty States:** Render clean empty state graphics when no routine or habits are defined.

## 6. Verification & Automated Tests
- Test that clicking check-in button dispatches correct API payload.
- Test that progress percentage updates reactively when habits are checked.

## 7. Definition of Done (DoD)
- [ ] Dashboard view unifies routine timeline and habits.
- [ ] Active time block highlighted based on current time.
- [ ] One-tap check-in responds with instant UI feedback.
